# Copy to .env.local for development. Nothing here is required to run `npm run dev` today —
# the commerce engine still runs on mock data until Supabase/Stripe are actually wired up
# (see docs/commerce/SUPABASE_SCHEMA_PROPOSAL.md and STRIPE_OBJECT_MAPPING.md).

# development | preview | production — explicit override; see src/commerce/env.ts.
# Leave unset locally; Next sets NODE_ENV for you.
# HUB_ENV=development

# The real production domain, once registered. Used for sitemap.xml, robots.txt, and absolute
# Open Graph URLs (src/app/site-config.ts). Falls back to a placeholder if unset.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://thehub-lloydswharf.example

# Where the /contact form's mailto: is addressed. Falls back to a placeholder if unset.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CONTACT_EMAIL=hello@thehub-lloydswharf.example

# off | availability | booking. Defaults to off. `availability` permits live reads but not
# holds; `booking` permits both. Do not enable either until the dedicated project is ready.
# HUB_BOOKING_MODE=off

# Server-only Supabase credentials. Never prefix the secret with NEXT_PUBLIC_. New projects
# should use an sb_secret_ key rather than the legacy service_role JWT.
# SUPABASE_URL=
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=

# Required before HUB_BOOKING_MODE=booking can be enabled. The database provider gives a
# deployment-safe shared limiter; the HMAC secret prevents storage of raw visitor addresses.
# The proxy header must be one guaranteed by the chosen host, not a client-controlled header.
# HUB_RATE_LIMIT_PROVIDER=database
# HUB_RATE_LIMIT_HMAC_SECRET=
# HUB_TRUSTED_PROXY_HEADER=x-vercel-forwarded-for

# Stripe is still pending and these remain server-only.
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
